# Python-generated files
__pycache__/
*.py[oc]
build/
dist/
wheels/
*.egg-info

# Virtual environments
.venv

# ---------------------------------------------------------------
# Project-specific
# ---------------------------------------------------------------

# Personal notes. These are thinking-out-loud documents -- idea.md is the
# original brief, plan.md is the design record including everything that went
# wrong, build.md is the step-by-step guide. They are written for the person
# building this, not for whoever clones it, and plan.md in particular is
# candid in a way that only makes sense in private.
idea.md
plan.md
build.md

# Secrets -- NEVER commit. If this leaks, rotate the key immediately.
# `.env.*` catches the copies people make and then forget about -- .env.backup,
# .env.old, .env.production -- while the `!` keeps the template, which holds no
# values and is meant to be shared.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Streamlit's OWN secrets file, which is not .env and lives in its own folder.
# It is where Streamlit's docs tell you to put API keys, so it is exactly the
# file someone adds at deploy time and never thinks to check.
.streamlit/secrets.toml

# Downloaded audio and raw transcription output.
# Large and fully regenerable from the source video, so we keep them
# out of git. data/processed/chunks.jsonl IS committed -- it is small
# and it is what makes the pipeline reproducible without re-transcribing.
data/audio/
data/raw/

# Embeddings are derived from chunks.jsonl and rebuild in about a minute,
# so there is nothing here worth versioning. The .meta.json sidecar names the
# chunks.jsonl that built the .npy -- it is meaningless without the .npy.
data/processed/embeddings*

# The language experiment's cached Groq responses. Regenerable, and they hold
# raw transcript text that the committed chunks.jsonl already contains.
eval/langtest_cache/

# Question -> search-form conversions (app/rag.py). Regenerable, and it holds
# whatever students typed, which is nobody else's business.
data/processed/convert_cache.json

# Notebook checkpoints
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# Claude Code's per-machine settings. The shared .claude/settings.json is worth
# committing someday; this one is personal -- it holds the permission prompts
# that were approved on THIS machine, and would override someone else's.
.claude/settings.local.json

# Insurance for the embedding model's 470 MB of weights. HF_CACHE_DIR points at
# E:/hf-cache today, outside the repo -- this only matters if someone edits it
# to a path inside, at which point a plain `git add .` would try to commit it.
hf-cache/

# Logs from streamlit / yt-dlp / ffmpeg runs.
*.log

# OS / editor cruft
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
